Cell["\<\
Each of these is written in the form a matrix product: (n), (n*m), (m) where \
the first (n) contain functions of eccentricity (\[Epsilon]) and eccentric \
anomaly (u) of the outer binary; the last (m) contain only functions of the \
eccentricity (\[Epsilon]) and eccentric anomaly (u) of the inner binary; for \
example:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9385064937803383`*^9, 3.938506688864098*^9}, {
